{"name":"Victoria","hex":"#564985","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Victoria","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Nymphaeaceae – certain waterlilies with very large flat leaves, native to the Amazon.","A taxonomic genus within the family Geometridae – certain moths native to Africa."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Roman goddess of victory, the counterpart of the Greek goddess Nike.","A female given name from Latin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Victoria"}],"entries":[{"title":"Queen Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Victoria was Queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland from 20 June 1837 until her death in 1901. Her reign of 63 years and 216 days, which was longer than those of any of her predecessors, constituted the Victorian era, a period of industrial, political, scientific, and military change within the United Kingdom marked by a great expansion of the British Empire. In 1876, the British parliament voted to grant her the additional title of Empress of India."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Queen_Victoria_by_Bassano.jpg/330px-Queen_Victoria_by_Bassano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Victoria"},{"title":"Victoria (state)","blocks":[{"text":"Victoria, commonly abbreviated as VIC, is a state in southeastern Australia. It is the second most populous state with a population of over 7 million, and the second-smallest, with a land area of 227,444 square kilometres (87,817 sq mi), making it the most densely populated state in Australia. Named in honour of Queen Victoria, Victoria was separated from New South Wales and established as a separate Crown colony in 1851, achieving responsible government in 1855."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Flag_of_Victoria_%28Australia%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Victoria_%28Australia%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_(state)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Sir_William_Beechey_%281753-1839%29_-_Victoria%2C_Duchess_of_Kent%2C_%281786-1861%29_with_Princess_Victoria%2C_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_407169_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-Sir_William_Beechey_%281753-1839%29_-_Victoria%2C_Duchess_of_Kent%2C_%281786-1861%29_with_Princess_Victoria%2C_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_407169_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Sir_William_Beechey_%281753-1839%29_-_Victoria%2C_Duchess_of_Kent%2C_%281786-1861%29_with_Princess_Victoria%2C_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_407169_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-Sir_William_Beechey_%281753-1839%29_-_Victoria%2C_Duchess_of_Kent%2C_%281786-1861%29_with_Princess_Victoria%2C_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_407169_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASir_William_Beechey_(1753-1839)_-_Victoria%2C_Duchess_of_Kent%2C_(1786-1861)_with_Princess_Victoria%2C_(1819-1901)_-_RCIN_407169_-_Royal_Collection.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Denning%2C_Stephen_Poyntz_-_Princess_Victoria_aged_Four_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Denning%2C_Stephen_Poyntz_-_Princess_Victoria_aged_Four_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Denning%2C_Stephen_Poyntz_-_Princess_Victoria_aged_Four_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Denning%2C_Stephen_Poyntz_-_Princess_Victoria_aged_Four_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Denning%2C_